#### CONCLUSION
1. Yanking every version of a gem whose record is <30 days old releases the
   name IMMEDIATELY (verified: claim succeeded ~14 min after the yank).
2. The claim REPLACES ownership: the original owner (omarqureshi, id 57418)
   vanished from owners.json; the claiming account (omarqureshitest, id 248742)
   is sole owner. No trace of the prior registration remains in the public API.
3. Yanked version numbers stay burned (0.0.0.pre.reserved.1 was not reusable).
4. Implication for the aws-* placeholders (created 2026-07-22): yanking all 8
   before ~2026-08-21 fully undoes the reservation. RISK: between yank and
   AWS's claim the names are open to anyone — execute as a coordinated
   handoff (AWS claims within minutes of the yank).
